    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32862" root="فت" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَتٌّ</span></b>  <i>A fissure</i> in a rock: (IAar, T, O, K:) as
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَتٌّ</span>: (IAar, T:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُتُوتٌ</span>. (IAar, T, O.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا فِى يَدِى مِنْكَ حَتٌّ وَلَا فَتٌّ</span> <i>There is not in
my hand, from thee, aught.</i> (O.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُولٰئِكَ أَهْلُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيْتٍ فَتٍّ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُتٍّ</span></b>  (Fr, T, O, K *) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِتٍّ</span></b> 
(Fr, T, K) <i>Those are the people of a house dispersed,</i> or <i>scattered,</i> (Fr, T, O, K. *)

